Hello,

Please prepare the Q3 2026 payroll reports for HANGS General Contracting LP: =
Form 941, the ESD unemployment insurance tax and wage report, the Paid Leave =
and WA Cares report, and the L&I workers' compensation quarterly report. Each=
 report is a draft for review; nothing is filed or paid until the review is d=
one.

Attached are the Q3 2026 payroll register, the federal tax deposit log and th=
e Q2 2026 year-to-date wages by employee. The register is the final export fr=
om the payroll system for the six Q3 paydays, July 10 to September 18. Every =
federal tax deposit for the quarter went through EFTPS.

Omar Rasmussen gave payroll a WA Cares exemption approval in July, and payrol=
l stopped that deduction from the July 24 payday.

Tomas Arvelo is paid through accounts payable, not payroll, for concrete fini=
shing at Tideflats Cold Storage.

Two more employees say WA Cares exemption applications have been sent in. No =
approval letter has arrived for either application, so payroll still takes th=
e WA Cares deduction from both employees' paychecks.

The other records are in the client folder: the employer accounts, the Q1 and=
 Q2 returns as filed, the 2026 rate records, the employee roster, the exempti=
on approvals on file, the payroll ledger accounts and the labor vendors paid.

Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS General Contracting LP
payroll@hangs-gc.example

